                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237871776",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198244548592",
                            "num_reviews": 59,
                            "playtime_forever": 1262,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 30,
                            "playtime_at_review": 1231,
                            "last_played": 1793764796
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I've played for much longer than steam says. Very enjoyable couch game. It is basically Dust 514 (rip) but less out of match content, less lore, less community, but a way bigger sandbox, has space / mixed maps, more game modes, IS PLAYABLE, and made by a group necessarily more reputable by not having done any sketchy things yet. Also this is an indie game, which is WILD given it could easily pass as a first party late 360 / early ps4 game. Grahpics are a touch crunchy, but enough that playing on a UHD projector makes it indistinguishable in level of detail from Blops Cold War. My only complaints are the single core CPU focus, and underwhelming mechs that move/feel like a swimming pool floater. The later of those two complaints is hardly a complaint when this game even has mechs in the tactical buffet of cost based vehicle loadouts. There is also a ninja-with-AT-artillery meta so fun that the devs had to add punching with your full loadout weight to balance it, the F-15T melee option. There was a GIf in the patch notes for that one which still makes me giggle a little.",
